$ floe check marks.yaml tab.yaml utf8.yaml
exit 1
--- stderr
marks.yaml:1:1: a byte order mark (U+FEFF) is here, which is read as a character: remove it, or write \ufeff in a double-quoted string where the text needs one
tab.yaml:8:11: a line of a | or > text begins with spaces and a tab, which YAML 1.2 reads as text, but floe as indentation, reading the lines after it otherwise: begin the line without the tab, or write the text's indentation after the | or > (like |2)
utf8.yaml:7:17: this byte is not UTF-8: save the file as UTF-8
$ floe render --out-dir $TMP/pages/marks.yaml marks.yaml
exit 1
--- stderr
marks.yaml:1:1: a byte order mark (U+FEFF) is here, which is read as a character: remove it, or write \ufeff in a double-quoted string where the text needs one
$ floe render --out-dir $TMP/pages/tab.yaml tab.yaml
exit 1
